    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d255">

                <pb facs="0484" n="360" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg360"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.48/578: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-08-06T19:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 6,
                                1923—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 6—1:43
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>205. My 204, August 6, 1 [<hi rendition="#italic">11</hi>] a.m. Adnan Bey<anchor
                        n="43" xml:id="d255-f1"/> informed me this morning that Red Crescent will be
                    unable to care for refugees if feeding is stopped by Near East and he urgently
                    requested Near East to continue such feeding. He furthermore urged me personally
                    to request Department to instruct American Chargé d’Affaires at Athens to make
                    representations to the Greek Government to evacuate the refugees as soon as
                    possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d255-f1" n="43" xml:id="d255-f1-content">
                <p>Vice President of the Turkish Grand National Assembly.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
